{"id":1375,"level":64,"name":"Взяття на проході","group":"Правила","format":30,"description":"When a pawn makes its very first move, it has a choice.<br />It can move one square or two squares at once!<br />You already know that.<br />But there&rsquo;s something else! <p>Pawns can speak a little bit of French&hellip;<br />They can capture<strong> en passant</strong>. This is French for &lsquo;in passing&rsquo;.<br />It is pronounced 'ahn pass-sahnt'.<br />One pawn can capture another without actually taking it!</p> <p>How does en passant capturing work?</p> <ul> <li>Only pawns can capture en passant. One pawn takes another.</li> <li>En passant capturing is done right after a pawn has moved up two squares in one turn.</li> <li>You pretend it only moved up one square. Your pawn captures diagonally and takes the other pawn.</li> <li>You have to this at once. If you don&rsquo;t, you lose the right to capture en passant.</li> </ul> <p><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />The black pawn makes a move. Can white capture en passant?<br />Click on the traffic lights to answer. Red = no, green = yes.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":24,"examples":[{"fen":"rnb1kbnr/pppp1ppp/4p3/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 1","pgn":"1. e5 d5 2. exd6 *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/4p3/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","pgn":"1. e5 f5 2. exf6 *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/1ppppppp/8/p7/3P4/8/PPP1PPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","pgn":"1. Nf3 a4 2. b4 axb3 *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3p4/8/3P4/PPP1PPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","pgn":"1. e4 d4 2. c4 dxc3 *","text":"","format":30}],"puzzles":[{"id":52675,"fen":"8/3p4/4p3/4P1k1/3PK3/7r/8/3R4 b - - 0 1","pgn":"1... d5+ {e5d6} *","format":30,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":53227,"fen":"3k4/4b3/8/3pp3/4P3/2NPK3/8/8 b - - 0 3","pgn":"1... d4+ {e4d5?} *","format":30,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":53228,"fen":"8/8/4k3/8/3pp3/4P3/2N